# Trivy accepted findings (B47). Each entry is a DOCUMENTED, deliberate exception — not blanket suppression.
# Consumed by the trivy-scan-job via --ignorefile /src/.trivyignore.

# ShadowRay — Ray Jobs API executes submitted code. DISPUTED by Anyscale as by-design (it's the product feature,
# not a bug); no Ray version patches it. Mitigated here by (1) network isolation — dashboard behind Keycloak
# forward-auth, Jobs API reachable only via cluster DNS, never the LAN — AND (2) Ray 2.56 built-in token auth
# (RAY_AUTH_MODE=token), enforced (a no-token request 401s). See k8s/ray/ray-head.yaml.
CVE-2023-48022

# Public GitHub repository is INTENTIONAL — this is a public homelab reference repo (weyland-lab). GIT-0001 flags
# "repo shouldn't be public"; that's the deliberate design, not a leak.
GIT-0001

# "Manage all resources" RBAC (KSV-0046) on Gatekeeper (OPA admission controller) + Kiali (Istio mesh viewer):
# both REQUIRE broad read/watch across resources to do their job (admission review / mesh topology). Scoped-down
# RBAC would break them. Accepted for a single-tenant LAN lab.
KSV-0046

# ---- B89 accepted (2026-07-18) ----

# readOnlyRootFilesystem (KSV-0118 = container, KSV-0014 = pod). ~193 hits — the B47 SYSTEMIC residual: blanket
# `readOnlyRootFilesystem: true` breaks the many workloads that write to their rootfs (caches, tmp, embedded DBs).
# Accepted repo-wide; revisit per-workload only if a specific one is hardened. Not per-item fixable on a LAN lab.
KSV-0118
KSV-0014

# Image runs as root (DS-0002) on the root-REQUIRED images: ranger, ray-head, weyland-dagster(+base, +feast). These
# need root at build/run (system pkgs, uid-agnostic caches); documented in the B47 pass. The non-root-capable images
# already carry USER 10001. Accepted for these; a new non-root-capable image should still fix it, not rely on this.
DS-0002

# Access to host network (KSV-0009) — ray-head.yaml. The persistent Ray head uses hostNetwork by design (stable
# ray.weyland.lab addressing for the rogueone edge worker). Intentional; see [[remote-training-rogueone]].
KSV-0009

# Access to host ports (KSV-0024) — coredns-lan.yaml. weyland-lan-dns binds hostPort 53 on the node (scoped to
# hostIP 192.168.1.243) — that IS the LAN DNS design + the fix for the CNI-DNAT capture incident (runbooks/lan-dns.md).
KSV-0024

# Manage Kubernetes networking (KSV-0056) — kiali.yaml. Kiali needs the networking RBAC to render Istio mesh
# topology (same rationale as its KSV-0046 above). Scoping it down breaks the mesh view. Accepted.
KSV-0056

# ConfigMap with secrets (KSV-0109) — now a FALSE POSITIVE on both hits, so blanket-accepted (B92, 2026-07-20):
# trino.yaml holds `${ENV:...}` refs (real creds in the `trino-secret` Secret), and ranger.yaml holds `@@TOKEN@@`
# placeholders (real creds sealed in `ranger-admin-secret`, substituted at startup by the render initContainer).
# Neither ships a real credential — trivy just can't tell a placeholder from a secret on a password-named key.
KSV-0109

# ---- B135 DoD Pillar 7 (2026-08-23) ----
# Privileged container (KSV-0017) on buildkitd ONLY. It performs the snapshot/overlay mounts an image build
# needs; daemonless BuildKit could not do them in an ephemeral step pod on this k3s cluster (EPERM even with
# privileged + AppArmor-unconfined + trusted-security), which is the whole reason a long-lived daemon exists
# (B57a, runbooks/woodpecker.md). Internal CI daemon, own namespace, reachable only via cluster DNS on a
# LAN-only single node.
#
# WHY HERE AND NOT INLINE: k8s/woodpecker/buildkitd.yaml already carries `# trivy:ignore:AVD-KSV-0017` (and
# -0014/-0118) above the resource. Those comments DO NOT WORK — verified 2026-08-23 against the pinned
# trivy 0.72.0 four ways: with the trailing prose stripped, with the AVD- prefix dropped, with no space after
# `#`, and relocated directly above the offending securityContext block. All three rules still fired every
# time. `.trivyignore` via --ignorefile is the mechanism that actually suppresses (which is why -0014 and
# -0118, listed above, do not appear in scan output while -0017 did). Treat the inline comments as prose
# documenting intent, NOT as suppression.
KSV-0017

# ---- B81 DoD close-out accepted (2026-09-02) ----
# CVE-2026-71211 — mlflow: SSRF via unvalidated AI Gateway secret (information disclosure), HIGH. NO UPSTREAM FIX:
# trivy reports fixed=None; the latest release 3.15.2 (2026-08-26) does not address it (release notes carry no
# security/SSRF/gateway entry), so there is nothing to bump to. Flagged on services/genre-trainer/requirements.txt,
# which is a mlflow CLIENT (tracking/logging only) — it never runs the AI Gateway server, so the vulnerable code
# path is not reachable from this component. The AI Gateway itself runs on the mlflow SERVER (`mlflow[gateway]`,
# /gateway/mlflow/…, k8s/mlflow/mlflow.yaml) whose only un-authenticated surface is the LAN NodePort :30500 — a
# deliberate, documented exposure on a $0 LAN-only single-node homelab (same posture that accepted the prior
# gateway SSRF window). Compensating: LAN-only, no external ingress, single tenant. REVISIT + bump both client
# and server the moment mlflow ships a patched release (as 3.14->3.15.1 cleared CVE-2026-64849).
CVE-2026-71211

# ---- 2026-10-02 DoD scan triage (golden-path fixtures, no upstream fix) ----
# Three npm advisories published Sep 3-18 against packages whose LATEST release is still the last affected version
# (checked 2026-10-02: braces 3.0.3, http-cache-semantics 4.2.0, node-forge 1.4.0 are each `npm view` latest and each
# advisory's `last_affected`), so there is nothing to bump to. They are flagged ONLY in golden-paths/*/package-lock.json:
# the B88 sample apps — CI-lane fixtures and ephemeral smoke Jobs, no durable deployment and no production data.
#   CVE-2026-93687  braces 3.0.3 — stack-exhaustion DoS on deeply nested patterns (build-time glob tooling; 8 samples).
#   CVE-2026-93748  http-cache-semantics 4.2.0 — max-stale can disclose cross-user cached responses (astro, angular).
#   CVE-2026-85393  node-forge 1.4.0 — RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature check accepts extra nested DigestAlgorithm
#                   (react-native dev tooling; nothing here verifies untrusted signatures).
# The same IDs are accepted in osv-scanner.toml. `exp:` makes each re-surface on 2027-01-02 — bump then if a fix exists.
CVE-2026-93687 exp:2027-01-02
CVE-2026-93748 exp:2027-01-02
CVE-2026-85393 exp:2027-01-02

# ---- 2026-10-09 B202 DoD scan triage (realm-of-agents) ----
# realm-of-agents/requirements.txt pins cryptography 49.0.0 because mlflow 3.15.x (matching the MLflow 3.15.1 server
# the Realm traces to) requires cryptography<50; the fix is 50.0.0. The CVE is in PKCS#7 EnvelopedData decryption, which
# the Realm never performs (it only makes TLS client calls). Lift it when the MLflow server and its clients move to 3.16+.
# Same ID in osv-scanner.toml. `exp:` re-surfaces it on 2027-01-09.
CVE-2026-69247 exp:2027-01-09
